.TH DS4-CTL 1 "August 2026" "ds4-ctl 1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ds4-ctl \- Control utility for the ds4-translator daemon
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ds4-ctl
[\fIcommand\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ds4-ctl
is the control interface for the \fBds4-translator\fR daemon. It communicates with the daemon via a Unix domain socket located at \fI/run/ds4-translator.sock\fR.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B status
Displays the current status of the daemon, including the physical controller event node, connection interface type, virtual emulation target type, and host client connection state.
.TP
.B set-type ds4
Changes the target virtual controller emulation type to a Sony DualShock 4.
.TP
.B set-type dualsense
Changes the target virtual controller emulation type to a Sony DualSense.
.TP
.B set-type none
Disables virtual controller emulation.
.TP
.B set-backend uhid
Changes the backend interface to `/dev/uhid` (requires daemon restart).
.TP
.B set-backend gadget
Changes the backend interface to `/dev/raw-gadget` (requires daemon restart).
.TP
.B help
Shows basic usage and command synopsis.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /run/ds4-translator.sock
The Unix domain socket used to communicate with the daemon.
.TP
.I /etc/ds4-translator.conf
The translator configuration file.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ds4-translator (1)
